SDL3 change the ScummVM DOS port needs so that a pre-SB16 Sound Blaster wired
to another 8-bit DMA channel than BLASTER's D still plays: some PnP and clone
chipsets (the YMF719's SB mode under 86Box asks for DMA 3 when BLASTER says D1
and DMA 1 when it says D3) request a channel the driver never programmed, so no
byte is transferred and no interrupt comes. OpenDevice now waits up to 250 ms
for the first interrupt; on a pre-SB16 card without one it tries the other
usable 8-bit channels (0, 1, 3; never the floppy controller's 2) and keeps the
first that interrupts, and when none does it goes back to BLASTER's channel and
logs "SB: card never interrupts (check BLASTER)", which the 16-bit path logs
too. The DMA set-up and the DSP start sequence moved into helpers unchanged.
The handler plays silence until the audio thread has mixed something, so the
wait is inaudible. The build defines DOS_SBProbeChecked, which build-dos.sh
looks for and the port links against.

Base: sdl3-irq-code.patch, sdl3-cpuid.patch, sdl3-sb-shutdown.patch and
sdl3-sb-open-fail.patch applied (~/opt/src/SDL3 branch dos-sb-probe =
dos-sb-shutdown f6cc527 + f5652a4 + d67c987). Apply after those four (git apply skips
this text):
  git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-irq-code.patch && git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-cpuid.patch \
    && git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-sb-shutdown.patch && git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-sb-open-fail.patch \
    && git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-sb-probe.patch

